---
title: "One lock byte: P1 leases it while P2 contends"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  s0: P1 idle
  s1: P1 tries
  s2: P1 waits
  s3: P1 holds the lease
  s4: P1 abandoned its wait
  s5: P1 idle, P2 holds the lock
  s6: P1 unlocks its abandoned lock
  s7: P1 waits, P2 holds the lock
  s8: P1 abandoned its wait, P2 holds the lock
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: TryLease
  s0 --> s2: WaitLease
  s1 --> s0: P1 process exits
  s1 --> s3: the lock is free
  s2 --> s0: P1 process exits
  s2 --> s3: the lock is granted
  s2 --> s4: the context ends
  s0 --> s5: P2 locks
  s3 --> s0: P1 process exits or Release
  s4 --> s0: P1 process exits
  s4 --> s6: the lock is granted
  s2 --> s7: P2 locks
  s5 --> s0: P2 process exits or P2 unlocks
  s5 --> s1: TryLease
  s5 --> s7: WaitLease
  s6 --> s0: unlock and drop the claim or P1 process exits
  s1 --> s5: P1 process exits or P2 has it, drop the claim
  s7 --> s2: P2 process exits or P2 unlocks
  s7 --> s5: P1 process exits
  s7 --> s8: the context ends
  s4 --> s8: P2 locks
  s8 --> s4: P2 process exits or P2 unlocks
  s8 --> s5: P1 process exits
